From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server, advapi32: a program started as another account inherits its starter's handles

A program started as another account inherited none of its starter's
handles. A service starts its helper on a person's desktop with
WTSQueryUserToken's token and CreateProcessAsUser, passing pipes whose values
it puts on the helper's command line; in a shared prefix the elevation broker
starts such a program as the person (1711), and it ignored bInheritHandles.
WireGuard for Windows' tray window ("wireguard.exe /ui 356 352 368 380",
started by its manager service) found no pipes there and ended at once, over
and over (i1010).

Now, as on Windows: with bInheritHandles the program inherits every
inheritable handle, or, with a PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_HANDLE_LIST (STARTUPINFOEX),
only the inheritable handles listed -- at the same values. advapi32 sends the
handles with the launch ticket (make_launch_ticket's optional request data: the
values, or ~0 alone for all; not declared as a VARARG, so the protocol is
unchanged), the server keeps their objects and puts them into the new
process's table when it names its ticket, before it opens anything.

Test: test/launchinherit-gate.sh (QA VM, as SYSTEM into a signed-in person's
session; test/runasuser-probe.c's new "inherit" mode): handle list, all, none,
the program running as the person. Fails with the old server; mutant
SG_MUTANT_LAUNCH_NO_INHERIT (server/token.c) fails it.
---
--- a/server/protocol.def
+++ b/server/protocol.def
